"Here's the `[[providers]]` section exactly as printed by `cat \"${REASONIX_HOME:-$HOME/.reasonix}/config.toml\"`:\n\n```toml\n[[providers]]\nname        = \"abb\"\nkind        = \"openai\"\nbase_url    = \"https://open.bigmodel.cn/api/coding/paas/v4\"\nmodels      = [\"glm-5.3-flash\"]\ndefault     = \"glm-5.3-flash\"\napi_key_env = \"ABB_AGENT_MODEL_API_KEY\"\nbalance_url = \"https://api.deepseek.com/user/balance\"   # optional; wallet-balance endpoint shown in the status bar\ncontext_window = 128000   # tokens; compaction triggers near this limit\nprice       = { cache_hit = 0.0028, input = 0.14, output = 0.28, currency = \"$\" }   # provider-wide fallback, per 1M tokens\n```\n\nThat's the only `[[providers]]` entry in the config. Note there's just one provider configured (`abb`, an OpenAI-compatible endpoint pointing at `open.bigmodel.cn`), with the API key stored indirectly via the `ABB_AGENT_MODEL_API_KEY` environment variable rather than in the file itself."